  "_comment": "The talk at the desk (docs/channel.md §16.7; Task 98). looks: what the presenters can wear and look like (each picked once from the league's seed and kept for its whole history): jackets, ties, hair colours and styles (short, long, bun). lines: each kind of line the presenters say, with the gesture the speaker makes while saying it (open: an open hand, making a point; point: pointing at the screens; laugh; both: both arms up; talk: just talking) and the ways of saying it, one picked by the segment's seed, {blanks} filled from real facts. draw to next: the stand-in lines (the latest result, a reaction, the leader, the next match) for the talk not written yet (gap clips, the tee-up, the welcome). matchWin to championsFirst (Task 99): the match talk, the interview's tee-up and wrap-up, the final round, and the talk opening the champions (the off-season's talk went in Task 207, the show having aired all it named). standingsLeader to teeUpKickoff (Task 101): the gap's clips (standings, scorers, upcoming; they never name a result) and the tee-up before each live match. welcomeHello to welcomeLeader (Task 106): the welcome that opens the channel's day. scorersPlayoffs and playoffsOtherSemi to playoffsReact (Task 155, Tom): in the playoffs the gap's standings clip becomes the playoffs (who's through, the final ahead; it reuses knockoutSemi and standingsFinal, voiced for every team) and the scorers clip names the playoffs' scorers too. The stand-in lines (draw to next) now only fill in when a talk has nothing to say. Task 131 (vision §12, the desk speaks, the graphics inform): each way is a pair, say (what's spoken and typed in the bubble: fixed, or naming one team as {team}, the fill named by the kind's subject, spoken as spokenTeam) and show (the graphic under the speaker, in capitals: any facts). So every spoken line can be made ahead, one clip per team where it names one. presenters (Task 132, Tom): who sits at the desk, left first (the left one speaks first): Hedrek Vosper, voiced by Raymond (ElevenLabs Library), and Ysolde Stavik, a woman (a scarf, a bun, earrings), voiced by Alice; look: which of the two seeded looks each wears (Hedrek keeps his). jingle (Task 137, Tom): the short trumpet tune each time the studio returns (as the glass sweep into the scene ends; at the Back to the studio bumper after an ad break), on the anthems' brass; notes are MIDI, beats at the bpm; with: other notes sounded with it (a chord); rest: a pause. Tom's tune: two quick chords and a pause, stepping down four times, then a quick run up in thirds to a held C major.",
